Sustainability Map MVP – Technical Implementation Spec

## 🔧 Overview

This MVP enables users to explore nearby sustainable locations (e.g., EV charging stations, organic stores, zero-waste shops) on a lightweight map UI, with basic filtering and information display.

**Tech Stack**
- Frontend: React / React Native or Web (Expo Web)
- Map Library: Leaflet.js (OpenStreetMap tiles)
- Data Source: Static JSON file (served locally or from CDN)
- Backend: None (MVP uses static data)

## 📍 Features (MVP Scope)

### ✅ Interactive Map
- Load map using Leaflet.js and OpenStreetMap tile layer.
- Auto-center to user’s location (fallback to default).
- Display pins based on location type (category).
- Custom pin icons (e.g., EV charger, zero-waste, etc.).

### ✅ Static Location Markers
- Read data from `/map/locations.json` at load.
- Markers display a popup with name, address, and link to navigation (Google Maps or Apple Maps).

### ✅ Basic Filtering
- Filter by category (`EV Charging`, `Organic Food`, `Recycling`, etc.).
- Filters applied locally on frontend; update visible pins dynamically.

### ✅ Business Profile (Popup Only)
- Name
- Address
- Category
- Description (short)
- Navigation button → opens Google Maps

